        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2849df63-713c-51cb-8d31-76ddc1960768",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Giovanni Furno, Vincenzo Bellini, Saverio Mercadante, Salvatore Agnelli, Niccolò Antonio Zingarelli, Gaetano Donizetti\n- Places: Capua, Naples, Palermo, Catania\n- Roles: composer, music teacher, opera composer, student\n\nFacts:\n- Giovanni Furno was born in Capua on January 1, 1748.\n- Giovanni Furno was an Italian composer and a famous music teacher.\n- Vincenzo Bellini was born on November 3, 1801.\n- Vincenzo Bellini was an Italian opera composer known for long-flowing melodic lines and was called \"the Swan of Catania.\"\n- Salvatore Agnelli was born in Palermo.\n- Salvatore Agnelli studied at the Naples Conservatory under Giovanni Furno, Niccolò Antonio Zingarelli, and Gaetano Donizetti.\n- Vincenzo Bellini and Saverio Mercadante were among Giovanni Furno's students.\n- Vincenzo Bellini died on September 23, 1835.\n- Giovanni Furno died in Naples on June 20, 1837.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
